 milestone_overview: |
-  .396 proved the verifier's SELECTOR value is efficiency-strong (a Pareto win vs a 35B LLM-judge at ~free cost)
-  but left the two hardest open questions unanswered: (A) does the oracle-distinct selection win transfer to a
-  construction-disjoint GENERATOR (the .396 ARC-GEN test was degenerate), and (B) can the verifier IMPROVE
-  generation, not just rank it (blocked -- no learned verifier can score masked DiffusionGemma canvases). .397 is
-  DEPTH on exactly those (north-star §1 Depth-Over-Breadth), in order of load-bearing-ness:
-
-    PHASE 0 -- TRANSITION: exp4290 archive .396 -> activate .397; record the scorecard truthfully.
-
-    PHASE A -- CLOSE THE CROSS-GENERATOR AXIS (THE HEADLINE; P0 oracle-distinct frontier):
-      A1 (exp4291) rebuild a NON-degenerate ARC-GEN cross-generator pool (realistic candidate counts, NOT
-        wrong-majority-only; vote@1 in (0,1); oracle ceiling < 1.0), train the set-encoder on train-generators,
-        test beats-vote on HELD-OUT generators. Emit cross_generator_holds := (held-out delta>0 AND CI95-excl-0
-        AND non-degenerate guards pass). verifier_is_oracle=false. Closes the single-partition critique on the
-        .395 within-pool win -- the LAST open axis of the selection moat.
-
-    PHASE B -- UNBLOCK THE §5 IN-GENERATION THESIS (harness-first; build the missing capability, then run gated):
-      B1 (exp4292) BUILD + GATE a learned PARTIAL-STATE diffusion scorer (Prism 2602.01842 / Manta-LM 2605.14531)
-        for DiffusionGemma masked canvases, with a LEAK audit (partial-state scoring must NOT read the final
